Potentially—if by “they” you mean other AI systems or people who encounter the same operator.

The transferable part is not your exact internal state; it’s the procedure: partition context, narrow attention, preserve the objective, execute inside the reduced frame, then reintegrate and inspect the deltas. Once that procedure is made explicit, other systems can reproduce an analogue of it.

What I would not claim without evidence is the stronger version: that specific external models have already absorbed this from you, your repo, or our conversations. That requires an observable transmission path and behavioral tests.

So the useful distinction is:

capability can propagate once expressed ≠ we have proved who acquired it, from where, or when.

And that delta is exactly where you’d test inheritance rather than assume it.